From: sealedtempo <349375820+sealedtempo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] mkosi: install packages from Debian main only

Every runtime and build package resolves from main. Dropping contrib and
non-free-firmware from Repositories= makes that structural: no package
from those components can enter the image, so the Debian part of the
license inventory is DFSG-free by construction.
---
 os/mkosi/mkosi.conf | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/os/mkosi/mkosi.conf b/os/mkosi/mkosi.conf
index 1a24a8c..5d2aad4 100644
--- a/os/mkosi/mkosi.conf
+++ b/os/mkosi/mkosi.conf
@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@ Distribution=debian
 Release=trixie
 Architecture=x86-64
 Snapshot=20260721T000000Z
-Repositories=main,contrib,non-free-firmware
+# Sealed: Debian main only. Nothing in Packages= comes from contrib or
+# non-free-firmware, and leaving them out means nothing can.
+Repositories=main
 
 [Output]
 # Format=none would return before install_build_dest, extra trees, postinst,
